---
export const title = 'Usage';
export const order = 100;
import DemoComponentCard from '../../../../components/DemoComponentCard.astro';
---

<DemoComponentCard lang={'html'}>
  <wc-chip>Chip</wc-chip>
</DemoComponentCard>

<DemoComponentCard lang={'html'}>
  <wc-chip dismissible value='Team'>
    <wc-icon slot=icon name="home"></wc-icon>
    Team
  </wc-chip>

  <wc-chip selected dismissible="true" value="Team">
    <wc-icon slot="icon" name="home"></wc-icon>
    Team
  </wc-chip>
</DemoComponentCard>

<p>
  A <code>selectable</code> chip is a toggle (a filter chip): its button tells assistive technology
  whether it is <code>selected</code> through <code>aria-pressed</code>. A plain chip is an action
  and has no pressed state. A standalone selectable chip does not toggle itself; set
  <code>selected</code> on <code>click</code>, or put the chips in a selecting
  <a href='../chip-set'><code>wc-chip-set</code></a>, which does.
</p>

<DemoComponentCard lang={'html'}>
  <wc-chip selectable selected>Team</wc-chip>
  <wc-chip selectable>Personal</wc-chip>
</DemoComponentCard>

<p>
  <code>skeleton</code> renders the chip as a placeholder while its content is not known yet. It is a
  look, not a busy state.
</p>

<DemoComponentCard lang={'html'}>
  <wc-chip skeleton>Loading</wc-chip>
</DemoComponentCard>
